  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Assistance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia supported the UN Access Support Unit to sustain the international humanitarian response in Gaza. Australian funding enabled more than 2,200 humanitarian workers to access Gaza through 4,439  humanitarian movement notifications. Australia&#x2019;s funding covered four months of operations for a 24/7 hotline assisting humanitarian personnel to enter, exit and move within the OPTs. Australia supported the ASU to coordinate 256 requests to import critical humanitarian items into Gaza, covering a total of more than 5 million items, including  for the health, food security, protection, water and sanitation sectors.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Economic policy reform and management and private sector development</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNOPS conducted a needs assessment of 900 fishermen in Gaza in an effort to facilitate the import of materials to repair boats and contribute to economic growth of the vital fisheries sector in Gaza. As a result of UNOPS&apos; intervention, outboard boat engines were officially imported to Gaza for the first time since 2007. The shipment of 12 engines of 25 HP was completed on 18 January, 2023. A second batch of fiberglass and related materials for repairing 7 boats were imported on 19 February, 2023. UNOPS&apos; teams provided coordination and monitoring activities for the imported.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
